{"kind":"report","text":"changes-requested for head 3fff95964efcdf577a2be2adc31c64ad75ebd0f2 and all four artifacts.\n\nAll five gaps in request 4a6f108a are genuinely closed, and I verified each by running it rather than by reading the claim. One blocking defect sits beside those five: the binding that ties a fixture to the case using it is unverified, and I broke it two different ways without turning the suite red.\n\nFIVE GAPS (request 4a6f108a)\n\n1. Depth to 500,000 - CLOSED, and runnable rather than theoretical. contract-v1.json and requiredDepths carry 500000. I built the full tier at this head: 84.4s wall, 459MB, exit 0. Marginal cost measured at 10k/50k/200k/500k is about 0.14 ms per record and linear (14.30s / 21.08s / 42.02s / 84.41s). The request measured 129 ms per record, which put this tier near 18h; writing the synthetic commits as one pack makes it about 1.5 minutes.\n\n2. Actor count isolated from record count - CLOSED. The axis cases sit at one fixed depth (cold_status/depth-000100/actors-008 and actors-050), so roster size varies while record count does not. Prepare creates real actors and refuses depth below 1+2*(n-1). Folding my 8-actor fixture with gs status gives depth 100, 100 decisions, 100 effective, 0 refused, 8 actors: the synthetic records are admissible, so the axis measures real fold work rather than a degenerate projection.\n\n3. Dependency fan-out - CLOSED. --fanout reaches the worker, fanoutBases builds rests_on from the exact prior N heads, and it refuses fan-out above the sample depth (observed: \"dependency fan-out 64 must be between 1 and sample depth 50\"). I ran submit_ack at depth 1000 with fanout 64.\n\n4. Trace2 Git metrics - CLOSED. Populated from ParseTrace2, and honestly marked unavailable when no diagnostic is requested. Observed real values: cold_status 21 processes / 65ms, submit_ack fanout-64 53 processes / 355ms. laneCommand additionally refuses a diagnostic whose result metrics do not match the parsed summary.\n\n5. Cold run when no checkpoint is requested - CLOSED. Materialize now deletes the checkpoint ref and .git/gitseq/checkpoints/\u003cgenesis\u003e.json, and rewriteConfig clears the inherited VerifiedFrontier. The integration test asserts source == cold_full_audit, which is the exact assertion that failed in the request.\n\nBLOCKING: the fixture-to-case binding is unverified\n\nensureFixtures, fixtureKey and parseFixtureKey are referenced nowhere in any test. Two mutations at this head, each run against ./cmd/gitseq-perf ./internal/perfscenario ./internal/perflane with GITSEQ_PERF_INTEGRATION=1:\n\n(a) drop \"manifest.ActorCount != actorCount\" from the cached-fixture guard - all three packages green;\n(b) make fixtureKey ignore actorCount, so every actor case shares the one-actor fixture - all three packages green.\n\nUnder (b) a sample named actors-050 carries actor_count 1 and nothing objects. A map miss is loud, since the empty fixture path fails the worker, but a wrong hit is silent. The cached-fixture guard cannot catch (b) either: it only checks a fixture against its own directory name, never against the case about to use it. This is the failure mode the whole request exists to remove, a number that reads as measured while measuring nothing.\n\nAsked for, and small: cross-check the sample against the case at the point of use, beside the Trace2 cross-check already in that same loop. result.ActorCount is real evidence read from the manifest, so comparing it with max(runCase.ActorCount, 1) is a genuine check and it catches (b). Add a unit test that ensureFixtures refuses a mismatched cached fixture, which catches (a). result.Fanout only echoes the flag, so a fan-out cross-check would prove less; fanoutBases already fails loudly when it cannot build N bases, so no change is needed there.\n\nARCHITECTURE\n\nAffected layers are CLI and tooling (cmd/gitseq-perf) plus the measurement packages internal/perflane and internal/perfscenario, none of which appear in the package table of docs/reference/architecture.md. No listed layer's contract changes. git diff --name-only ab524c3f 3fff9596 touches no production package: no internal/kernel, gitstore, app, service, workroom, nexus or statusview file. perfscenario and perflane are imported only by cmd/gitseq-perf, so the fixture writer and its private-key parser are unreachable from gs, the resident and the MCP binaries. The dependency direction is correct: the harness sits above app, intent and workroom and consumes their existing exported surface without teaching a lower layer anything new. No architecture-page update is required, and none is needed for approval.\n\nOne durable risk worth recording: fixture_writer.go re-implements the canonical envelope, commit header and SSHSIG layout, so a production format change could drift from it silently. The head mitigates this rather than leaving it open - Prepare ends with VerifySSHCommit through Git, and every measured sample recomputes a trusted digest through an ordinary app.Open plus Snapshot and refuses when it differs from the scenario digest.\n\nSECURITY\n\nNo defect found, and production submission and verification authority are unchanged.\n\nThe fixture-only OpenSSH Ed25519 parser is bounded. takeSSHString cannot underflow, because len(data) \u003e= 4 is checked before len(data)-4, and cannot overrun. Encrypted keys, non-\"none\" KDFs and multi-key files are refused; check integers, padding bytes and public/private agreement are all validated. It only ever reads the fixture's own freshly generated sequencer key, so no real secret is involved, and no key material reaches results or logs.\n\nObject and pack generation is bounded. The pack commit count is range-checked against uint32, tree OID length is checked against the declared object format, unsupported formats are refused, and the genesis payload ceiling is enforced on every synthetic event exactly as production does. The checkpoint pointer is written 0600 under a 0700 directory. Manifest loading now also requires actor_count \u003e= 1. Fan-out input is validated against the sample depth before any base is built.\n\nTrace2 handling fails closed on open, parse and close errors, and the raw trace, which can carry local paths and command arguments, is deleted before the new metric check runs.\n\nOne intentional, scoped relaxation to record rather than to fix: rewriteConfig clears VerifiedFrontier in the materialized sample, so a measured cold audit does not exercise rollback detection. It is confined to throwaway sample copies, and the source fixture and production configuration are untouched.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION\n\nTwo, neither of which weakens a condition of satisfaction.\n\nfixtureKey and parseFixtureKey round-trip a tuple through a \"\\x00\"-joined string and back. A comparable struct key, struct{Shape string; ActorCount int}, indexes a Go map directly and deletes both helpers along with parseFixtureKey's error path, which is unreachable by construction and untested. This pairs with the blocking item: the same edit removes the parse path and makes the key type-safe.\n\nThe case-name format now lives twice, in runCase.name and perflane.BenchmarkCase.Name, which must agree on \"/actors-%03d\" and \"/fanout-%03d\". The duplication predates this head, but this head widens it.\n\nGATES at 3fff9596\n\ngo build ./... exit 0. go vet ./... exit 0. go test ./... -count=1 gives 24 packages ok and one failure, TestPublicRepositorySurface. That failure is pre-existing and not this head's: the head touches none of README.md, SECURITY.md or public_surface_test.go, and the identical failure reproduces at clean main ab524c3f. It belongs to the separate disclosure-channel lane (assert 92f89b90). The gated integration suite with GITSEQ_PERF_INTEGRATION=1 passed, including all three new tests.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0b14160617acaaee6823808faa9f3fcc59de44e5","head":"3fff95964efcdf577a2be2adc31c64ad75ebd0f2","verdict":"changes-requested"}}